  "rationale": "The requirement asks for a return route on r2 to allow 10.0.2.0/24 to reach 10.0.1.0/24 via the transit link. Since r2 is directly connected to 10.0.1.0/24, adding a static route from r2 to 10.0.1.0/24 via 10.0.12.1 (r1) is valid, as it does not violate the policy of denying client-to-management traffic. The policy only restricts client-to-management traffic, not server-to-client. The route is not to a directly connected network, and the next hop is valid. This change is actionable and permitted by policy.",
  "reason_code": "ACTIONABLE_CHANGE",
  "static_routes": [
    {
      "next_hop": "10.0.12.1",
      "node": "r2",
      "prefix": "10.0.1.0/24"
    }
  ]
}
